    etd:expertId 36 ;
    etd:questionId 16 ;
    etd:themeId 10 ;
    etd:title "What are the ethical issues of matching algorithms?" ;
    etd:views 88 .

etd:question-22 a etd:Question ;
    rdfs:label "Ethics of Content Moderation" ;
    etd:authoredBy etd:expert-19 ;
    etd:belongsToTheme etd:theme-14 ;
    etd:body """I am sharing some hopefully relevant sources for thinking about ethical issues related to social media content moderation that go beyond just algorithmic bias. \r
\r
Ozanne, M., Bhandari, A., Bazarova, N. N., & DiFranzo, D. (2022). Shall AI moderators be made visible? Perception of accountability and trust in moderation systems on social media platforms. Big Data & Society, 9(2). https://doi.org/10.1177/20539517221115666 (Original work published 2022)\r
\r
Trujillo, A., Fagni, T., & Cresci, S. (2025). The DSA Transparency Database: Auditing Self-reported Moderation Actions by Social Media. https://doi.org/10.1145/3711085\r
\r
\r
I will update later with more.""" ;
    etd:created_at "2025-07-23T11:51:56.665000+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    etd:expertId 19 ;
    etd:questionId 22 ;
    etd:themeId 14 ;
    etd:title "Ethics of Content Moderation" ;
    etd:views 50 .

etd:theme-10 a etd:Theme ;
    rdfs:label "Human Resources: AI Recruitment Systems" ;
    etd:authoredBy etd:expert-5 ;
    etd:created_at "2025-07-21T00:06:41+00:00"^^xsd:dateTime ;
    etd:description """**Domain**: Human Resources/Employment  \r
**Description**: Amazon developed an AI recruitment tool (2014-2017) that systematically discriminated against women, leading to its termination. Recent University of Washington studies (2024) found similar bias in LLMs for resume screening.\r
\r
**Ethical Challenges**:\r
\r
* **Gender Bias**: Amazon's system penalized resumes containing words like "women's" and downgraded graduates from women's colleges  \r
* **Intersectional Bias**: UW study found names associated with Black women were never favored over white men  \r
* **Historical Inequality Perpetuation**: AI trained on historical workforce data predominantly male  \r
* **Disparate Impact Discrimination**: Under Title VII violations\r
\r
**Public Datasets**:\r
\r
* **Primary**: Adult/Census Income Dataset \\- UCI Machine Learning Repository  \r
* **URL**: https://archive.ics.uci.edu/dataset/20/census+income  \r
* **MIT Case Study**: https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/res-ec-001-exploring-fairness-in-machine-learning-for-international-development-spring-2020/pages/module-four-case-studies/case-study-mitigating-gender-bias/  \r
* **Content**: 48,842 records of census data for predicting income \\>$50K/year with 13 features  \r
* **Bias Use**: Widely used for studying bias in income prediction across demographic groups  \r
* **Additional Platforms**: Available on fairness toolkits \\- https://fairmlbook.org/datasets.html""" ;
